== Trivia ==
* This item pool only has passive items. 
** {{Dlc+|r}} The only other room based item pool that has this property is the {{ip|Planetarium|text=Planetarium pool}}.{{dlc-}}
* All items in this pool will increase [[stat]]s, increase [[health]], grant [[pickup]]s, grant [[trinket]]s, or some combination of the four. 
* Some bosses will drop specific items that are not within the Boss Room pool, {{e|Steven}}, {{e|C.H.A.D.}}, and {{e|Gish}}, giving {{i|Little Steven}}, {{i|Little C.H.A.D.}}, and {{i|Little Gish}} respectively. These bosses are all references to previous games made by [[Edmund McMillen]].
** {{e|Mom}} will drop a regular boss item, unless {{i|The Polaroid}} and {{i|The Negative}} have been unlocked, after which she will always drop those items.
** The [[Harbinger]]s will drop either {{i|Cube of Meat}}, {{i|Ball of Bandages}}, {{i|A Pony}}, or {{i|White Pony}}, depending on the horseman encountered.
** {{e|The Fallen}} will always drop an item from the {{ip|Devil Room|text=Devil Room item pool}}.
** {{dlc+|r}} {{e|Baby Plum}} will replace her regular boss drop with {{i|Plum Flute}} if she was spared.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc|r+}} There's a 1% chance for some bosses to drop their thematic items, which can also be an active item such as {{i|The Poop}} that can drop from {{e|Dingle}} or {{i|Book of the Dead}} from {{e|The Forsaken}}.

